  "content": "<p><strong>Unit 10 - Word Problems — Title &amp; Goal</strong><br />Comprehensive lesson covering Unit 10 - Word Problems for SAT Math preparation.</p>\n\n\n<h3>Key idea</h3>\n<p>Read the idea and scan the rules. Focus on how the symbols behave.</p>\n<p><strong>Example 1</strong><br/>\nA number increased by 7 is 20. Find the number.  </p>\n<p>Let <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> = the number.  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow></math>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>Example 2</strong><br/>\nA rectangle has length 3 more than twice its width. If the perimeter is 42, find dimensions.  </p>\n<p>Let width = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>w</mi></mrow></math>, length = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>42</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mn>2</mn><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>42</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mn>6</mn><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></math>\n<p>Then <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></math>.<br/>\nRectangle: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>×</mi><mn>15</mn></mrow></math>.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p>Distance = rate × time.  </p>\n<p><strong>Example 3</strong><br/>\nA car travels 60 miles in the same time a train travels 100 miles. If the train is twice as fast, find car’s speed.  </p>\n<p>Let <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></math> = car speed. Train speed = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></math>.<br/>\nTime = distance/rate.  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>50</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>\n<p>Contradiction → no solution. Check: maybe train is <em>not exactly twice</em> but “20 mph faster.”  </p>\n<p><strong>Revised Problem</strong><br/>\nCar: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></math>, Train: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow></math>, Times equal.  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>\n<p>Cross-multiply: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mn>60</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1200</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mn>40</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1200</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow></math>.<br/>\nCar = 30 mph, Train = 50 mph.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p>Work rate = 1 / (time to finish).  </p>\n<p><strong>Example 4</strong><br/>\nAlice can paint a room in 4 hours, Bob in 6 hours. How long together?  </p>\n<p>Rates: Alice = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>, Bob = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></math>. Together = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></math>.<br/>\nSo time = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>12</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2.4</mn></mrow></math> hours.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>Example 5</strong><br/>\nA 20-liter solution is 25% acid. How much water to add to make it 10% acid?  </p>\n<p>Acid = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>0.25</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>20</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math> liters.<br/>\nFinal solution: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> liters, still 5 acid.  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0.10</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mi>x</mi><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mn>0.1</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow></math>\n<p>Add 30 liters water.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>Example 6</strong><br/>\nFind three consecutive integers whose sum is 96.  </p>\n<p>Let numbers = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>96</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>96</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>93</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>31</mn></mrow></math>\n<p>Numbers: 31, 32, 33.</p>\n<hr/>\n<ul>\n<li>Define variables before writing equations.  </li>\n<li>Watch out for <strong>“at least,” “at most”</strong> (inequalities).  </li>\n<li>Always answer in the <strong>context of the problem</strong> (no raw variables).  </li>\n<li>Plug answer choices back in if stuck (backsolving).  </li>\n</ul>\n<hr/>\n<p>1) A number decreased by 8 is 15. What is the number?<br/>\n2) A rectangle has width <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>w</mi></mrow></math> and length <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>w</mi></mrow></math>. If area = 75, find <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>w</mi></mrow></math>.<br/>\n3) A plane flies 600 miles in the same time a car drives 200 miles. If plane speed is 4 times car speed, find speeds.<br/>\n4) Two workers can finish a job in 5 hours together. If one works twice as fast as the other, how long alone for each?<br/>\n5) A 40-liter mixture is 30% sugar. How much pure sugar to add to make it 50% sugar?  </p>\n<hr/>\n<p>1) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>23</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>2) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>3) Car = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></math>, Plane = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></math>. <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>600</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mn>150</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></math>. Contradiction → recheck wording. Likely: “Plane is 300 mph faster.”<br/>\nTry: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>600</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>300</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></math>. Cross multiply: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>600</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>300</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>⇒</mo><mn>600</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>000</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mn>400</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>000</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn></mrow></math>. Car = 150 mph, Plane = 450 mph.  </p>\n<p>4) Let slow = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></math>, fast = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></math>. Together rate = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></math>. Time = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></math>. So slow = 15 hrs, fast = 7.5 hrs.  </p>\n<p>5) Sugar initially = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>0.3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>40</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></math>. Add <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> sugar → total sugar = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>, total volume = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>40</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>.<br/>\nEquation: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></math>\n<p>.<br/>\nAdd 16 liters sugar.</p>\n\n<h3>Quick practice</h3>\n<p>Try these on your own. Check your steps, not just the final answer.</p>\n\n<h3>Mixed practice set</h3>\n<p>These mix everything above. Time yourself and reflect on any mistakes.</p>\n",
